WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.635
-My first guest
is a World Series champion,

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.804
an Emmy-winning baseball analyst
and color commentator,

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.572
and a very successful
entrepreneur.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:08.174
He stars as a guest judge

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.943
on a new episode of the popular
show "Shark Tank,"

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.346
which you can now see on demand
and on Hulu.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.948
Here is Alex Rodriguez!

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:19.918
Hey, Alex, welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:21.954
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:24.424
You were on our show
back in April,

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.459
which was pretty early on
in quarantine.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.027
So thanks for coming on then.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:31.598
Who'd thought we'd still be here
nine months later on Zoom?

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.966
-It's crazy, Jimmy.
It's always so great to see you.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.102
I see you've upgraded --
you're now on your set.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.504
I've upgraded to my bar.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.173
-That's how long
this has gone on.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.508
-That's exactly
where most people are, yeah.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.310
Yeah, you were in your office
last time, right?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.778
-Yeah, I'm still in my office.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.280
[ Both laugh ]
I made it a bar.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.582
-Exactly right.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.484
I have so many things
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.818
But I was very curious,

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.487
'cause you were in Times Square
for New Year's Eve.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.056
I saw you guys
with Ryan Seacrest,

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.658
and Jennifer was awesome --
her performance.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.493
Happy New Year, by the way.
-Same to you.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.496
What was it like to be
in Times Square with no people?

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:05.564
-Jimmy, it was crazy.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.233
I've been to Times Square
a million times,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:11.103
but to be there where --
no fans on New Year's,

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:12.872
I mean, it seems like
for the last hundred years,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.040
you've millions of people
out there,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.143
and hopefully, God willing,
for the next hundred years,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.310
you have millions of people.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.713
But Jennifer killed it.
It was awesome.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:21.881
But Jennifer
did have a great slide.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.983
I thought that was my job.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.384
-Dude, yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.752
I'm used to seeing you sliding,
yeah.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.421
She had one of the best slides.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.823
It was -- I mean,
whatever she does always --

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.092
she does it the best,
always goes everywhere.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.027
I just saw
you guys are gonna be --

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.029
you're headed off to Washington.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.032
-She's going to be performing
at the inauguration.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.967
-Jimmy, it's been
such a crazy year for her --

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.769
I mean, so amazing,
so many blessings.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.139
But to think,
in the span of 12 months,

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.175
she's done the Super Bowl,
New Year's,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.544
and now the inaugural --
it's unbelievable.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.280
And what's interesting
is she's most nervous

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.815
about Washington, D.C.,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.850
because of the responsibility.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.553
And she wants more than
anything, like all of us,

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.523
to bring people together,
to inspire.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.225
And, you know, music and sports
does that better than anything.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.960
And she has
something really cool.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.829
You're going to be surprised.
You're going to love it.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.163
-Really?
-You're going to love it.

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:12.631
-'Cause she always does --
alright, good, good, good.

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.400
I don't want to know.
This is so good.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.402
Hey, 2021 --

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.871
do you think you guys are
finally going to get married?

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.506
[ Chuckling ]
What do you think?

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.775
-You know,
we tried twice in 2020.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.678
-I know.
-We got bit twice by COVID-19.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.012
-Yeah.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:28.981
-You know, they say in baseball,
third time's the charm.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.249
So let's -- let's...

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.383
-There we go.
-Let's hope it's...year.

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:32.652
-Alright, good.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.220
I want to talk about
the new season of baseball.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.990
What can you tell us
about the upcoming season?

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.692
-Well, I'm excited.
I mean,

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.694
we're supposed to start
Opening Day, April 1st.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.596
Baseball and sports -- I mean,
we just need it so much.

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.733
We saw football this weekend --
it's so much fun.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.703
But, again, music and sports
bring people together

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.605
more than anything
around the globe.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.574
And Commissioner Manfred
just said

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.409
that he expects a full season --

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.544
not sure
what the fan situation will be.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:01.013
But Yankees are on fire,
Mets are on fire.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.849
It's gonna be an awesome year.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.651
And I can't wait for 162,
a full season.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.620
-Right? Yeah.
People like seeing you.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.589
I mean, that's why -- I mean,
I see you on "Shark Tank,"

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.058
because you're -- you know what
you're talking about.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.827
You've built
a giant business empire.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.695
Is it -- Have you always been
into business,

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:21.167
or is this a thing post-sports?

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.635
-Yeah,
ever since I was 10 years old,

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:26.239
I've had
two big kind of goals, as --

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.506
I call them the two B's --
right? --

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:28.841
baseball and business.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:31.277
And I wanted to be like
my father, an entrepreneur.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.045
He also loved baseball.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.780
And I've studied it
for a long time.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.916
We're lucky
we have an incredible team.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.052
We've done some awesome things
in 2020

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.588
through
a very, very difficult time.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:44.023
We've given tons back
to the community.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.191
-Yeah.
-But we're happy

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.727
we're taking a public company,
hims &amp; hers,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.995
one of the great telemedicine
companies that we have,

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:51.464
going public.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.666
And then, we're taking another
one public later in the year.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.634
So it's been a very active,
busy year.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.936
We've been growing a lot,

00:03:56.936 --> 00:04:00.206
and excited to do more
and give back more.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.907
-Why do you like doing
"Shark Tank"?

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.209
-I like it for several reasons.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.777
Number one, I feel like,
on Friday nights,

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.312
America is getting
their MBA in business.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.613
That's number one.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.749
-Number two,
it's done a lot of social good.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:14.253
It's deployed over $100 million,
over 25,000 jobs.

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:16.122
My daughters, Natasha and Ella,

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.524
ever since they were, like,
little, little, little girls,

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.127
I always used to
make them pitch to us

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.862
and tell us about
their business ideas.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.130
-Alright, I'm trying to think
of any ideas I can pitch you,

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.067
'cause I always try
to pitch you ideas.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:31.704
I have one idea
for a silent glass.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.605
So, if you're having a cocktail,

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:37.777
I don't want to hear
the ice clink around, you know?

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.478
Alright.
That's one idea.

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.747
But I don't know how you do it
or if anyone needs it,

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.784
but, hey, I like options.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.719
Do I have any other bad ideas?

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:49.255
I have an idea for Oreo.
-Okay.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.690
-I think Oreo should come out

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.725
with cookie dough in the middle
of the --

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.127
instead of the creme filling.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:56.795
If Oreos...
-Okay.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:58.331
-Would...
-You're getting warmer.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:02.067
-Okay.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.369
Alright.
I'm trying to think -- Oh!

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.138
Then I thought
of another cookie idea

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.740
where the inside
is powdered milk.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.377
So, when you eat the cookie,
it turns into milk and cookies.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.312
It's gross -- never mind.
Okay.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.114
I want to --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.850
That was the reaction --
-You saved the worst for last.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.052
It was great.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:21.620
-That's the reaction
I want to see, man.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.322
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.524
Here's Alex Rodriguez
in "Shark Tank."

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:26.792
Take look at this.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.595
-So there's two rules
in investing, as I see it.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.530
Rule number one
is don't lose money.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.865
-Right.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.900
-Rule number two is
don't forget rule number one.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.069
-Yeah.
-Okay?

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.637
So I'm going to make
this investment

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.305
as convertible debt.
-Okay.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:43.175
I'm going to offer you
$200,000 for 20%.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.044
When you hit your 1.8...
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.013
-...it will convert into equity.
-Okay.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:49.115 line:0%
-That's my offer.
-Okay.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:52.552 line:0%
-You understand
the dilution of that.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.920 line:0%
-I do.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.521
-Alex Rodriguez, everybody!

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.823
Catch him in an all-new episode
of "Shark Tank,"

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.625
now on demand and on Hulu.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.361
Alex and I are playing
the "Singing Whisper Challenge"

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:03.463
when we come back.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.031
It's going to be fun.
Stick around.

